==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{recons|freusaną|lang=gem-pro}}, whence also Old English {{term|freosan|frēosan|lang=ang}}, Old Saxon and Old High German {{term|friosan|lang=goh}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{recons|prews-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|prus-|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Verb===
{{head|non|verb}} (''strong conjugation:'' [[fraus]] – [[frusu]] – [[frosit]])

# to [[freeze]]

====Descendants====
* Icelandic: {{l|is|frjósa}}
* Faroese: {{l|fo|frosin}} (adjective from the past participle)
* Norwegian (nynorsk): {{l|nn|frjosa}}
* Danish: {{l|da|fryse}}
* Swedish: {{l|sv|frysa}}

